{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/6d0f6dwf","slideIndex":5,"position":{"left":76,"top":610,"width":1110,"height":58},"text":"Balanced tests make Macro = Weighted. Single-label Micro P/R/F1 = Accuracy. These are not independent evidence.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":20,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#5A6962","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/6bd914","slideIndex":5,"text":"Source: https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/model_evaluation.html#classification-metrics. Precision=TP/(TP+FP). Recall=TP/(TP+FN). F1=2PR/(P+R). Micro equals Accuracy in single-label classification. Weighted and Macro coincide under the balanced supports used here."}
